<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.relay.fm/focused/268">On this episode of <em>Focused</em></a>, Mike and I welcome historian Liz Covart, host of <em>Ben Franklin&#8217;s World</em>. We talk about making time for reading and research when you don&#8217;t have a finished piece to show for it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Liz explains where robots help her find research and where she keeps the thinking and interview questions to herself. I share how I dictate book notes while the thought is still fresh. We also talk about why a new app can wait until the current project is finished.</p>
